        ["Northbridge v1 is stipulated to materially rank recruitment candidates for an ordinary private employer. Its case dossier contains a supported non-prohibited-use analysis, Annex III classification, Section 2 evidence, Article 17 processes, Annex IV technical documentation, recorded Annex VI checks, a complete signed declaration, accessible digital CE marking and the appropriate provider registration. Within these stated checks, a supported readiness conclusion can be recorded, with ongoing obligations and named owners."],
        ["Harbour v1 is stipulated to require sector third-party assessment. Its certificate refers to v0 and the assessor's relevant scope has not been verified. Mark the release **not ready on the stated evidence**: resolve competence/scope and version coverage, and obtain the applicable assessment evidence. A launch promise is not an Article 46 sector derogation. A separate sector-law review remains necessary."],
        ["If Northbridge later changes its intended purpose or makes an unplanned compliance-affecting modification, review classification, provider role and reassessment; do not recycle v1's conclusion automatically. A public-authority customer has its own applicable registration and impact-assessment duties. These are distinct from the private-employer case assumptions."],
        ["Use three outcomes: **ready for the specified checked scope**, **not ready because a required condition is unmet**, or **needs further review because decisive facts or interpretation are unresolved**. Record each conclusion's facts, dated sources, evidence links, conditions, decision owner and next action. Unknowns should remain visible. Passing this lesson demonstrates reasoning practice, not certification of an actual product."],
